  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1024 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nTemperatures will gradually warm throughout the week as high\npressure maintains its dominance across Middle Tennessee. By\nweek's end, the upper ridge will flatten out, and this will enable\nus to transition a more unsettled weather pattern by the weekend.\nAt this time, it appears that our next rain chances will arrive on\nHalloween, but better rain chances will develop Saturday night and\nSunday and continue into at least the early part of next week. So\nwhile we expect drought continues to worsen even more this week,\nperhaps the increased probability of meaningful rainfall can at\nleast put the breaks on any additional worsening after this week.",
